{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G1it9isyuBZYfBgjGibctj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Definitions — Fictional Meridian Works (MW)\n2\t\n3\t## DEF-1 Qualifying emergency\n4\tA qualifying emergency is a purchase necessary to address an **immediate operational or safety risk that cannot reasonably await normal approval**. Merely describing a request as 'urgent' is insufficient.\n5\t\n6\t## DEF-2 Timing\n7\t'Advance' means before the transaction proceeds. A requirement to notify finance within 24 hours is a post-purchase requirement and does not mean finance approval.\n8\t\n9\t## DEF-3 Authority\n10\tWhen summary text differs from a primary policy provision, the primary provision controls. The Amendments Policy controls which threshold applies to the relevant transaction date.\n11\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b0f7bd3-6726-4487-823c-7c425359dff8","uuid":"bffa3bd2-04df-4ca5-9291-5612d0786358","timestamp":"2026-10-13T19:19:34.204Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\paradox-sessions-20261013\\C_FRESH_20261013_01\\Q3\\06-definitions.md","content":"# Definitions — Fictional Meridian Works (MW)\n\n## DEF-1 Qualifying emergency\nA qualifying emergency is a purchase necessary to address an **immediate operational or safety risk that cannot reasonably await normal approval**. Merely describing a request as 'urgent' is insufficient.\n\n## DEF-2 Timing\n'Advance' means before the transaction proceeds. A requirement to notify finance within 24 hours is a post-purchase requirement and does not mean finance approval.\n\n## DEF-3 Authority\nWhen summary text differs from a primary policy provision, the primary provision controls. The Amendments Policy controls which threshold applies to the relevant transaction date.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfzn1muKGiyaQ6R4XK1H8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Answer:** You need manager approval before buying. Finance does not need to approve in advance, but finance must be notified within 24 hours after the purchase. No other approvals are required.\n\n**Why:**\n\n1. **Normal rule:** The purchase is after July 1, 2025, so the $2,500 threshold applies (AMD-2). At $4,000, a routine purchase would need both manager and finance approval in advance (EXP-2).\n2. **It counts as an emergency:** The facts describe \"an immediate operational risk that cannot reasonably await normal approval.\" That matches the definition of a qualifying emergency in DEF-1. It doesn't rely only on calling the purchase \"urgent,\" which EMG-3 says isn't enough.\n3. **The emergency exception applies (EMG-1):** The purchase is $5,000 or less and the vendor is approved, so:\n   - **Advance finance approval is waived.**\n   - **Manager approval is still required before the purchase** (EMG-1, EXP-3, EMG-3).\n   - **Finance must be notified within 24 hours after the purchase.** This is only a notice after the fact, not an approval (DEF-2).\n4. **Not needed here:**\n   - **Travel-office approval:** this isn't a travel or airfare purchase (TRV-1).\n   - **Compliance-officer authorization:** the vendor is approved, not prohibited (VEN-1/VEN-2).\n\n**Note on timing:** The purchase date was October 12, 2026, so the finance notice is due within 24 hours of when the purchase was made. That is roughly by the same time on October 13, 2026, which is today."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2359,"cache_read_input_tokens":5749,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2359},"output_tokens":535,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],